IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition (SSO informal consolidation, version in force 6/5/2026 to 20/10/2026):
-- Part 4, Division 5 -- Debentures (ss 93 to 100; ss 97 to 99, 101 to 106 repealed), and the repealed Divisions 5A and 6 (ss 106A to 120). Layer 1, part agent sgj.
-- Source file lines 10296-10470. The text is a rendering of the Act, not the official text.
--
-- HOW IT IS MODELLED. One company and one issue of debentures at a time. Decision functions answer MAYBE BOOLEAN (JUST TRUE yes, JUST FALSE the text's own no, NOTHING "the text does not say").
-- Whether an instrument is a "debenture" is s 4(1)'s (the keel's `s 4(1) "debenture"`): these functions take the answer as a fact ("the company issues debentures").
-- GIVES to the keel (PLAN.md table A, s 4(1) "branch register" (b)): `s 93(8) the register is a branch register of holders of debentures kept pursuant to section 93`.
-- The clock of the traces of s 93(2) counts days; that of ss 93(5) and (6), which the one-month outer limit of s 93(7) governs, counts months.

§ `Section 93: register of debenture holders and copies of trust deed`

DECLARE `s 93 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 93(1) keep a register of holders of the debentures at the registered office or at some other place in Singapore`
    `s 93(2) lodge with the Registrar notice of the place where the register is kept, or of the change of place`
    `s 93(3) keep the register open to inspection`
    `s 93(5) supply a copy of the register of holders of debentures`
    `s 93(6) forward a copy of the trust deed`

-- s 93(1): a company which issues debentures (not being debentures transferable by delivery) must keep the register at the registered office or at some other place in Singapore.
-- The parenthesis limits who the duty is addressed to and says no "only": for debentures transferable by delivery the duty is not covered (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (c)).
-- src:10300 | 93.—(1) Every company which issues debentures (not being
-- src:10301 | debentures transferable by delivery) must keep a register of holders
-- src:10302 | of the debentures at the registered office of the company or at some
-- src:10303 | other place in Singapore.
@ref s 93(1) (src:10300-10303)
GIVEN `the company issues debentures, as section 4(1) defines the word` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the debentures are debentures transferable by delivery` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company keeps a register of holders of the debentures` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the register is kept at the registered office of the company or at some other place in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 93(1) the company has kept the register as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company issues debentures, as section 4(1) defines the word`) OR `the debentures are debentures transferable by delivery`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every company which issues debentures (not being debentures transferable by delivery)" -- a scope limit with no "only"
    ELSE IF `the company keeps a register of holders of the debentures` AND `the register is kept at the registered office of the company or at some other place in Singapore`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must keep a register of holders of the debentures at the registered office of the company or at some other place in Singapore" -- a duty: the provision's own question

-- s 93(1) as a regulative rule: a standing duty with no time limit and no consequence of its own (NOTES.md, Rules with no breach path).
@ref s 93(1) (src:10300-10303)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 93 act`
`s 93(1) the company must keep a register of holders of the debentures` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 93(1) keep a register of holders of the debentures at the registered office or at some other place in Singapore`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 93(1) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not keep a register of holders of the debentures at the registered office or at some other place in Singapore" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md) [class: maintenance; see notes]

-- s 93(2): within 7 days after the register is first kept at a place other than the registered office, and within 7 days after any change in the place, lodge notice with the Registrar.
-- src:10305 | (2) Every company must within 7 days after the register is first kept
-- src:10306 | at a place other than the registered office lodge with the Registrar
-- src:10307 | notice of the place where the register is kept and must, within 7 days
-- src:10308 | after any change in the place at which the register is kept, lodge with
-- src:10309 | the Registrar notice of the change.
@ref s 93(2) (src:10305-10309)
GIVEN `the day the register was first kept at a place other than the registered office, or the day the place at which the register is kept changed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 93(2) the last day for lodging notice of the place or of the change` MEANS
    `period: the last day of a period after` `the day the register was first kept at a place other than the registered office, or the day the place at which the register is kept changed` 7 Days

@ref s 93(2) (src:10305-10309)
GIVEN `the day the register was first kept at a place other than the registered office, or the day the place at which the register is kept changed` IS A DATE
      `the day the notice was lodged` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 93(2) the notice was lodged within 7 days` MEANS
    IF `the day the notice was lodged` AT MOST (`s 93(2) the last day for lodging notice of the place or of the change` `the day the register was first kept at a place other than the registered office, or the day the place at which the register is kept changed`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must within 7 days after the register is first kept at a place other than the registered office lodge with the Registrar notice" -- a period the text fixes in its own words (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a))

@ref s 93(2) (src:10305-10309)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 93 act`
`s 93(2) the company must lodge notice of the place or of the change within 7 days` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 93(2) lodge with the Registrar notice of the place where the register is kept, or of the change of place`
    WITHIN 7
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not lodge with the Registrar notice of the place where the register is kept, or of the change of place, within 7 days"

-- s 93(4): when a register is deemed to be duly closed. "deemed ... if" gives a sufficient condition and does not say "only" (fork F-j93-1).
-- src:10317 | (4) For the purposes of this section, a register is deemed to be duly
-- src:10318 | closed if closed in accordance with the provisions contained in the
-- src:10319 | constitution or in the debentures or debenture stock certificates, or in
-- src:10320 | the trust deed or other document relating to or securing the
-- src:10321 | debentures, during such periods (not exceeding in the aggregate
-- src:10322 | 30 days in any calendar year) as is therein specified.
@ref s 93(4) (src:10317-10322)
GIVEN `the register is closed in accordance with the provisions contained in the constitution, in the debentures or debenture stock certificates, or in the trust deed or other document relating to or securing the debentures` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the register is closed during the periods specified in those provisions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the aggregate number of days in the calendar year for which the register is closed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 93(4) the register is deemed to be duly closed` MEANS
    IF    `the register is closed in accordance with the provisions contained in the constitution, in the debentures or debenture stock certificates, or in the trust deed or other document relating to or securing the debentures`
      AND `the register is closed during the periods specified in those provisions`
      AND `the aggregate number of days in the calendar year for which the register is closed` AT MOST 30
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a register is deemed to be duly closed if closed in accordance with ... (not exceeding in the aggregate 30 days in any calendar year)" -- a deeming "if" gives a sufficient condition; the subsection does not say a register closed otherwise is not duly closed

-- s 93(3): open to inspection of a registered holder of debentures and of any holder of shares, except when duly closed; contents.
-- src:10311 | (3) The register must except when duly closed be open to the
-- src:10312 | inspection of the registered holder of any debentures and of any
-- src:10313 | holder of shares in the company and must contain particulars of the
-- src:10314 | names and addresses of the debenture holders and the amount of
-- src:10315 | debentures held by them.
@ref s 93(3) (src:10311-10315)
GIVEN `the person is a registered holder of debentures of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a holder of shares in the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the register is duly closed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 93(3) the register must be open to the inspection of the person` MEANS
    IF `the register is duly closed`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The register must except when duly closed be open to the inspection of ..."
    ELSE IF `the person is a registered holder of debentures of the company` OR `the person is a holder of shares in the company`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the subsection names "the registered holder of any debentures and ... any holder of shares" and does not say "only"

@ref s 93(3) (src:10311-10315)
GIVEN `the register contains particulars of the names and addresses of the debenture holders` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the register contains particulars of the amount of debentures held by them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 93(3) the register has the content the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the register contains particulars of the names and addresses of the debenture holders` AND `the register contains particulars of the amount of debentures held by them`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must contain particulars of the names and addresses of the debenture holders and the amount of debentures held by them" -- a duty: the provision's own question

@ref s 93(3) (src:10311-10315)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 93 act`
`s 93(3) the company must keep the register open to inspection` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 93(3) keep the register open to inspection`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 93(3) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not keep the register open to the inspection of the registered holders of debentures and of the holders of shares" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md) [class: maintenance; see notes]

-- s 93(5): a registered holder of debentures and a holder of shares must, at the holder's request, be supplied with a copy of the register or any part, on payment of $1 for every page or part.
-- src:10326 | (5) Every registered holder of debentures and every holder of
-- src:10327 | shares in a company must, at the request of the holder of debentures
-- src:10328 | or shares, be supplied by the company with a copy of the register of
-- src:10329 | the holders of debentures of the company or any part thereof on
-- src:10330 | payment of $1 for every page or part thereof required to be copied,
-- src:10331 | but the copy need not include any particulars as to any debenture
-- src:10332 | holder other than the debenture holder’s name and address and the
-- src:10333 | debentures held by the debenture holder.
@ref s 93(5) (src:10326-10333)
GIVEN `the person is a registered holder of debentures of the company or a holder of shares in the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has requested a copy of the register or part of it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has paid $1 for every page or part of a page required to be copied` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 93(5) the company must supply the person with a copy of the register` MEANS
    IF `the person is a registered holder of debentures of the company or a holder of shares in the company` AND `the person has requested a copy of the register or part of it` AND `the person has paid $1 for every page or part of a page required to be copied`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "must, at the request of the holder, be supplied ... on payment of $1 for every page or part thereof" -- the duty is limited by the holder's request and the payment; without them the text is silent (fork F-j93-4)

@ref s 93(5) (src:10326-10333)
GIVEN `the number of pages, or parts of a page, required to be copied` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 93(5) the most the company may require to be paid for the copy of the register` MEANS
    `the number of pages, or parts of a page, required to be copied` TIMES 1   -- "payment of $1 for every page or part thereof required to be copied"

@ref s 93(5) (src:10326-10333)
GIVEN `the particulars are of a debenture holder, and are other than the debenture holder's name and address and the debentures held by the debenture holder` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 93(5) the copy must include the particulars` MEANS
    IF `the particulars are of a debenture holder, and are other than the debenture holder's name and address and the debentures held by the debenture holder`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the copy need not include any particulars as to any debenture holder other than the debenture holder’s name and address and the debentures held"
    ELSE NOTHING      -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection says nothing of the name, address and holding, which the copy of the register contains

-- s 93(6): a copy of any trust deed must be forwarded to a holder of the debentures at the holder's request on payment of $3 or such less sum as the company fixes, or $1 a page where the copy has to be specially made.
-- src:10335 | (6) A copy of any trust deed relating to or securing any issue of
-- src:10336 | debentures must be forwarded by the company to a holder of those
-- src:10337 | debentures at the holder’s request on payment of the sum of $3 or
-- src:10338 | such less sum as is fixed by the company, or where the copy has to be
-- src:10343 | specially made to meet the request on payment of $1 for every page or
-- src:10344 | part thereof required to be copied.
@ref s 93(6) (src:10335-10344)
GIVEN `the person is a holder of the debentures` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has requested a copy of the trust deed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has paid the sum the subsection allows the company to require` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 93(6) the company must forward the copy of the trust deed to the holder` MEANS
    IF `the person is a holder of the debentures` AND `the person has requested a copy of the trust deed` AND `the person has paid the sum the subsection allows the company to require`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "must be forwarded ... to a holder of those debentures at the holder's request on payment of the sum of $3" -- without the request and the payment the text is silent (fork F-j93-4)

@ref s 93(6) (src:10335-10344)
GIVEN `the copy has to be specially made to meet the request` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of pages, or parts of a page, required to be copied` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 93(6) the most the company may require to be paid for the copy of the trust deed` MEANS
    IF `the copy has to be specially made to meet the request`
    THEN `the number of pages, or parts of a page, required to be copied` TIMES 1   -- "where the copy has to be specially made to meet the request on payment of $1 for every page or part thereof"
    ELSE 3                                                                         -- "the sum of $3 or such less sum as is fixed by the company"

-- s 93(5) and (6) as regulative rules. The time limit is that of s 93(7): "a reasonable time (but not more than one month) after a request". Only the one-month outer limit can be traced; the clock counts months after the request.
@ref s 93(6) (src:10335-10344)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 93 act`
`s 93(6) the company must forward the copy of the trust deed within one month` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 93(6) forward a copy of the trust deed`
    WITHIN 1
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not forward the copy of the trust deed within one month after the request"

-- s 93(7): the offence of refusing inspection or a copy, or not forwarding a copy within a reasonable time (not more than one month).
-- src:10346 | (7) If inspection is refused, or a copy is refused or not forwarded
-- src:10347 | within a reasonable time (but not more than one month) after a
-- src:10348 | request has been made pursuant to this section, the company and
-- src:10349 | every officer of the company who is in default shall be guilty of an
-- src:10350 | offence.
@ref s 93(7) (src:10346-10350)
GIVEN `the day the request was made` IS A DATE
      `the day the copy was forwarded` IS A DATE
      `the copy was forwarded within a reasonable time after the request` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 93(7) the copy was forwarded within the time the subsection allows` MEANS
    IF `the copy was forwarded within a reasonable time after the request` AND (`the day the copy was forwarded` AT MOST (`period: the last day of a period after` `the day the request was made` 1 Months))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within a reasonable time (but not more than one month) after a request has been made" -- a period the text fixes in its own words (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a)); what is a reasonable time is taken as a fact

@ref s 93(7) (src:10346-10350)
GIVEN `inspection is refused` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a copy is refused` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a copy is not forwarded within a reasonable time, and in any case not within one month, after the request` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 93(7) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` MEANS
    IF    (`inspection is refused` OR `a copy is refused` OR `a copy is not forwarded within a reasonable time, and in any case not within one month, after the request`)
      AND (`the person is the company` OR `the person is an officer of the company who is in default`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If inspection is refused, or a copy is refused or not forwarded within a reasonable time ..., the company and every officer of the company who is in default shall be guilty of an offence" -- an element is unmet (split site (i), fork line F-j93-3)

-- s 93(7) states no penalty; s 93(9) does, for a failure to comply with the section.
@ref s 93(7) (src:10346-10350)
GIVEN `inspection is refused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 93(7) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction under this subsection` MEANS
    NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): subsection (7) creates the offence and states no fine; subsection (9) states one for a failure to comply with the section (fork F-j93-3)

-- s 93(8): a branch register of debenture holders kept outside Singapore is part of the company's register; Division 4 of Part 5 applies with adaptations.
-- src:10352 | (8) A company which issues debentures may cause to be kept in any
-- src:10353 | place outside Singapore a branch register of debenture holders which
-- src:10354 | is deemed to be part of the company’s register of debenture holders
-- src:10355 | and Division 4 of Part 5 applies with such adaptations as are
-- src:10356 | necessary to and in relation to the keeping of a branch register of
-- src:10357 | debenture holders.
@ref s 93(8) (src:10352-10357)
GIVEN `the company issues debentures, as section 4(1) defines the word` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 93(8) the company may cause a branch register of debenture holders to be kept outside Singapore` MEANS
    IF `the company issues debentures, as section 4(1) defines the word`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A company which issues debentures may cause to be kept in any place outside Singapore a branch register" -- a grant limited by its own wording (the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1; fork F-j93-5)

@ref s 93(8) (src:10352-10357)
GIVEN `the register is a register of debenture holders kept in a place outside Singapore by a company which issues debentures` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 93(8) the register is a branch register of holders of debentures kept pursuant to section 93` MEANS
    IF `the register is a register of debenture holders kept in a place outside Singapore by a company which issues debentures`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- the answer the keel's `s 4(1) "branch register"` limb (b) asks for (PLAN.md table A)
    ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks of a register kept outside Singapore

@ref s 93(8) (src:10352-10357)
GIVEN `the register is a branch register of holders of debentures kept pursuant to section 93` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 93(8) the branch register is deemed to be part of the company's register of debenture holders` MEANS
    IF `the register is a branch register of holders of debentures kept pursuant to section 93`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a branch register of debenture holders which is deemed to be part of the company’s register"

@ref s 93(8) (src:10352-10357)
GIVEN `the register is a branch register of holders of debentures kept pursuant to section 93` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 93(8) Division 4 of Part 5 applies, with the adaptations necessary, to the keeping of the branch register` MEANS
    IF `the register is a branch register of holders of debentures kept pursuant to section 93`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Division 4 of Part 5 applies with such adaptations as are necessary to and in relation to the keeping of a branch register of debenture holders"

-- s 93(9): the offence of failing to comply with the section, with its fine and a default penalty.
-- src:10359 | (9) If a company fails to comply with this section, the company and
-- src:10360 | every officer of the company who is in default shall be guilty of an
-- src:10361 | offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding
-- src:10362 | $1,000 and also to a default penalty.
@ref s 93(9) (src:10359-10362)
GIVEN `the company fails to comply with section 93` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 93(9) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` MEANS
    IF `the company fails to comply with section 93` AND (`the person is the company` OR `the person is an officer of the company who is in default`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company fails to comply with this section, the company and every officer of the company who is in default shall be guilty of an offence" -- an element is unmet (split site (i), fork line F-j93-3)

@ref s 93(9) (src:10359-10362)
GIVEN `the company fails to comply with section 93` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 93(9) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    IF `s 93(9) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` `the company fails to comply with section 93` `the person is the company` `the person is an officer of the company who is in default` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    --                          fine, months, both, default penalty
    THEN JUST (Penalty OF 1000, 0, FALSE, TRUE)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states a penalty only for the person it makes guilty

§ `Section 94: specific performance of contracts`

-- src:10366 | 94. A contract with a company to take up and pay for any
-- src:10367 | debentures of the company may be enforced by an order for specific
-- src:10368 | performance.
@ref s 94 (src:10366-10368)
GIVEN `the contract is a contract with a company to take up and pay for debentures of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 94 the contract may be enforced by an order for specific performance` MEANS
    IF `the contract is a contract with a company to take up and pay for debentures of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A contract with a company to take up and pay for any debentures of the company may be enforced by an order for specific performance" -- a grant limited by the kind of contract (fork F-j94-1)

§ `Section 95: perpetual debentures`

-- src:10372 | 95. A condition in any debenture or in any deed for securing any
-- src:10373 | debentures whether the debenture or deed is issued or made before or
-- src:10374 | after 29 December 1967 is not invalid by reason only that the
-- src:10375 | debentures are thereby made irredeemable or redeemable only on the
-- src:10376 | happening of a contingency however remote or on the expiration of a
-- src:10377 | period however long, despite any rule of law or equity to the contrary.
@ref s 95 (src:10372-10377)
GIVEN `the condition is in a debenture or in a deed for securing debentures, whether issued or made before or after 29 December 1967` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the only ground relied on for invalidity is that the debentures are thereby made irredeemable, or redeemable only on the happening of a contingency however remote or on the expiration of a period however long` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 95 the condition is invalid by reason only that it makes the debentures irredeemable or redeemable only on a contingency or after a period` MEANS
    IF    `the condition is in a debenture or in a deed for securing debentures, whether issued or made before or after 29 December 1967`
      AND `the only ground relied on for invalidity is that the debentures are thereby made irredeemable, or redeemable only on the happening of a contingency however remote or on the expiration of a period however long`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A condition in any debenture or in any deed for securing any debentures ... is not invalid by reason only that the debentures are thereby made irredeemable ... despite any rule of law or equity to the contrary"
    ELSE NOTHING      -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by reason only" -- another ground of invalidity is not covered

§ `Section 96: reissue of redeemed debentures`

-- s 96(1): the power to reissue, unless a contrary provision or a manifested intention to cancel; and the reissue is not the issue of a new debenture for a limit on the amount or number.
-- A function named for a power whose gate is closed with "unless" keeps JUST FALSE (the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 2).
-- src:10381 | 96.—(1) Where a company has redeemed any debentures whether
-- src:10382 | before or after 29 December 1967 —
-- src:10387 | (a) unless any provision to the contrary, whether express or
-- src:10388 | implied, is contained in the constitution or in any contract
-- src:10389 | entered into by the company; or
-- src:10391 | (b) unless the company has, by passing a resolution to that
-- src:10392 | effect or by some other act, manifested its intention that the
-- src:10393 | debentures are to be cancelled,
-- src:10395 | the company has and is deemed always to have had power to reissue
-- src:10396 | the debentures, either by reissuing the same debentures or by issuing
-- src:10397 | other debentures in their place but the reissue of a debenture or the
-- src:10398 | issue of one debenture in place of another under this subsection,
-- src:10399 | whether the reissue or issue was made before or after that date, is not
-- src:10400 | to be regarded as the issue of a new debenture for the purpose of any
-- src:10401 | provision limiting the amount or number of debentures that may be
-- src:10402 | issued by the company.
@ref s 96(1) (src:10381-10402)
GIVEN `the company has redeemed debentures, whether before or after 29 December 1967` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a provision to the contrary, express or implied, is contained in the constitution or in a contract entered into by the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has, by passing a resolution to that effect or by some other act, manifested its intention that the debentures are to be cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 96(1) the company has power to reissue the redeemed debentures` MEANS
    IF NOT `the company has redeemed debentures, whether before or after 29 December 1967`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a company has redeemed any debentures" -- a scope limit with no "only"
    ELSE IF (NOT `a provision to the contrary, express or implied, is contained in the constitution or in a contract entered into by the company`) AND (NOT `the company has, by passing a resolution to that effect or by some other act, manifested its intention that the debentures are to be cancelled`)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless any provision to the contrary ... is contained in the constitution or in any contract ...; or unless the company has ... manifested its intention that the debentures are to be cancelled" -- the gate is closed with "unless"

@ref s 96(1) (src:10381-10402)
GIVEN `the issue is a reissue of a debenture, or the issue of one debenture in place of another, under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 96(1) the reissue is regarded as the issue of a new debenture for the purpose of a provision limiting the amount or number of debentures` MEANS
    IF `the issue is a reissue of a debenture, or the issue of one debenture in place of another, under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is not to be regarded as the issue of a new debenture for the purpose of any provision limiting the amount or number of debentures that may be issued by the company"
    ELSE NOTHING      -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the text speaks of a reissue or substitute issue under this subsection

-- src:10406 | (2) After the reissue the person entitled to the debentures has and is
-- src:10407 | deemed always to have had the same priorities as if the debentures
-- src:10408 | had never been redeemed.
@ref s 96(2) (src:10406-10408)
GIVEN `the debentures have been reissued under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 96(2) the person entitled to the debentures has the same priorities as if the debentures had never been redeemed` MEANS
    IF `the debentures have been reissued under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "After the reissue" -- without a reissue the subsection is silent

-- src:10410 | (3) Where a company has either before or after 29 December 1967
-- src:10411 | deposited any of its debentures to secure advances on current account
-- src:10412 | or otherwise, the debentures are not deemed to have been redeemed
-- src:10413 | by reason only of the account of the company having ceased to be in
-- src:10414 | debit while the debentures remain so deposited.
@ref s 96(3) (src:10410-10414)
GIVEN `the debentures were deposited by the company to secure advances on current account or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the debentures remain so deposited` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the only ground for treating the debentures as redeemed is that the account of the company has ceased to be in debit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 96(3) the debentures are deemed to have been redeemed by reason of the account having ceased to be in debit` MEANS
    IF    `the debentures were deposited by the company to secure advances on current account or otherwise`
      AND `the debentures remain so deposited`
      AND `the only ground for treating the debentures as redeemed is that the account of the company has ceased to be in debit`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the debentures are not deemed to have been redeemed by reason only of the account of the company having ceased to be in debit while the debentures remain so deposited"
    ELSE NOTHING      -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by reason only" and "while the debentures remain so deposited"

§ `Sections 97 to 99: repealed by S 236/2002`

-- src:10416 | 97. [Repealed by S 236/2002]
-- src:10418 | 98. [Repealed by S 236/2002]
-- src:10420 | 99. [Repealed by S 236/2002]

§ `Section 100: power of Court in relation to certain irredeemable debentures`

-- s 100(3): subsection (1) does not apply to a debenture offered to the public for subscription or purchase.
-- src:10461 | (3) Subsection (1) does not apply in relation to any debenture that is
-- src:10462 | offered to the public for subscription or purchase.
@ref s 100(3) (src:10461-10462)
GIVEN `the debenture is offered to the public for subscription or purchase` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 100(3) subsection (1) applies to the debenture` MEANS
    IF `the debenture is offered to the public for subscription or purchase`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not apply in relation to any debenture that is offered to the public for subscription or purchase"
    ELSE NOTHING      -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection says nothing of a debenture not so offered

-- s 100(2): subsection (1) does not affect any power to vary rights or accept a compromise or arrangement.
-- src:10456 | (2) Subsection (1) does not affect any power to vary rights or accept
-- src:10457 | any compromise or arrangement created by the terms of the
-- src:10458 | debentures or the relevant trust deed or under a compromise or
-- src:10459 | arrangement between the borrowing corporation and creditors.
@ref s 100(2) (src:10456-10459)
GIVEN `the power is a power to vary rights or accept a compromise or arrangement, created by the terms of the debentures or the relevant trust deed or under a compromise or arrangement between the borrowing corporation and creditors` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 100(2) subsection (1) affects the power` MEANS
    IF `the power is a power to vary rights or accept a compromise or arrangement, created by the terms of the debentures or the relevant trust deed or under a compromise or arrangement between the borrowing corporation and creditors`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not affect any power to vary rights or accept any compromise or arrangement"
    ELSE NOTHING      -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection says nothing of any other power

-- s 100(1): the Court may order that the security be enforceable, on the application of the trustee (or, with no trustee, a holder), if the Court is satisfied of (a), (b) and (c).
-- A function named for a power whose "if" gate fails answers NOTHING (the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1; fork F-j100-1). Where subsection (3) excludes the debenture the answer is the text's no.
-- (b) "not more than 60%": 100 times the sum likely to be brought is at most 60 times the principal sum of moneys outstanding.
-- src:10424 | 100.—(1) Despite anything in any debenture or trust deed, the
-- src:10425 | security for any debentures which are irredeemable or redeemable
-- src:10426 | only on the happening of a contingency shall, if the Court so orders,
-- src:10427 | be enforceable, immediately or at such other time as the Court directs
-- src:10428 | if on the application of the trustee for the holders of the debentures or
-- src:10429 | (where there is no trustee) on the application of the holder of any of
-- src:10430 | the debentures the Court is satisfied that —
-- src:10435 | (a) at the time of the issue of the debentures the assets of the
-- src:10436 | corporation which constituted or were intended to
-- src:10437 | constitute the security therefor were sufficient or likely
-- src:10438 | to become sufficient to discharge the principal debt and
-- src:10439 | any interest thereon;
-- src:10441 | (b) the security, if realised under the circumstances existing at
-- src:10442 | the time of the application, would be likely to bring not
-- src:10443 | more than 60% of the principal sum of moneys outstanding
-- src:10444 | (regard being had to all prior charges and charges ranking
-- src:10445 | pari passu if any); and
-- src:10447 | (c) the assets covered by the security, on a fair valuation on the
-- src:10448 | basis of a going concern after allowing a reasonable
-- src:10449 | amount for depreciation are worth less than the principal
-- src:10450 | sum and the borrowing corporation is not making
-- src:10451 | sufficient profit to pay the interest due on the principal
-- src:10452 | sum or (where no definite rate of interest is payable)
-- src:10453 | interest thereon at such rate as the Court considers would
-- src:10454 | be a fair rate to expect from a similar investment.
@ref s 100(1) (src:10424-10454)
GIVEN `the debentures are irredeemable or redeemable only on the happening of a contingency` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is made by the trustee for the holders of the debentures or, where there is no trustee, by the holder of any of the debentures` IS A BOOLEAN
      `at the time of the issue the assets which constituted or were intended to constitute the security were sufficient or likely to become sufficient to discharge the principal debt and any interest` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sum the security, if realised under the circumstances existing at the time of the application, would be likely to bring, regard being had to all prior charges and charges ranking pari passu` IS A NUMBER
      `the principal sum of moneys outstanding` IS A NUMBER
      `the assets covered by the security, on a fair valuation on the basis of a going concern after allowing a reasonable amount for depreciation, are worth less than the principal sum` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the borrowing corporation is not making sufficient profit to pay the interest due on the principal sum or, where no definite rate of interest is payable, interest at a fair rate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the debenture is offered to the public for subscription or purchase` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 100(1) the Court may order that the security be enforceable` MEANS
    IF `the debenture is offered to the public for subscription or purchase`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): s 100(3) "Subsection (1) does not apply in relation to any debenture that is offered to the public for subscription or purchase"
    ELSE IF    `the debentures are irredeemable or redeemable only on the happening of a contingency`
           AND `the application is made by the trustee for the holders of the debentures or, where there is no trustee, by the holder of any of the debentures`
           AND `at the time of the issue the assets which constituted or were intended to constitute the security were sufficient or likely to become sufficient to discharge the principal debt and any interest`
           AND (`the sum the security, if realised under the circumstances existing at the time of the application, would be likely to bring, regard being had to all prior charges and charges ranking pari passu` TIMES 100) AT MOST (`the principal sum of moneys outstanding` TIMES 60)
           AND `the assets covered by the security, on a fair valuation on the basis of a going concern after allowing a reasonable amount for depreciation, are worth less than the principal sum`
           AND `the borrowing corporation is not making sufficient profit to pay the interest due on the principal sum or, where no definite rate of interest is payable, interest at a fair rate`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "shall, if the Court so orders, be enforceable ... if on the application ... the Court is satisfied that (a) ...; (b) ...; and (c) ..." -- a power whose "if" gate is unmet (fork F-j100-1: the other reading is JUST FALSE)

